/*!
  \page example_cu_kdtree_page Fitting with kd-tree queries in CUDA kernels

  \section cu_kdtree_intro_sec Introduction

  This example fits a plane (Ponca::MeanPlaneFit) at every point of a planar point cloud, in a CUDA kernel. The
  neighbors are collected on the GPU by querying a kd-tree built on the CPU and copied to the device (see
  \ref ponca_gpu_spatial). The helper functions copying the buffers of the tree are defined in
  `examples/cuda/cuda_utils.cu`.

  To compile and run the example:
  \code{.sh}
  cmake --build build --target cuda_fit_plane_kdtree
  ./build/examples/cuda/cuda_fit_plane_kdtree
  \endcode

  \section cu_kdtree_code Source code

  \include cuda/ponca_fit_kdtree.cu
 */
